# Table Header Divider Spacing

All directory/table cards must use the same divider + spacing between the
`CardHeader` (search/toolbar) and the table body. Keep it consistent with every
other workspace table (orders, customers, invoices, items, vehicles, etc.).

## Rules

- The table `Card` **must** set `gap-0`. The shadcn `Card` defaults to
  `flex flex-col gap-6`, which inserts a 24px gap between the header's `border-b`
  divider and the table. Use `className="mt-6 gap-0"`.
- The toolbar `CardHeader` owns the divider via `border-b` and uses exactly
  `className="gap-3 border-b py-4 pb-3"`.
- The table (`DataTable` / loader / empty state) renders **directly** after the
  `CardHeader`. Do **not** add top margin/padding (e.g. `mt-*`, `pt-*`) or a
  spacer wrapper between the divider and the table.
- The footer/pagination row gets its own divider with `border-t px-6 py-4`.

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — gap-0 keeps the table flush beneath the divider
<Card className="mt-6 gap-0">
  <CardHeader className="gap-3 border-b py-4 pb-3">
    <TableDirectoryToolbar /* search + columns */ />
  </CardHeader>
  <DataTable /* ... */ />
  <div className="flex ... border-t px-6 py-4">{/* pagination */}</div>
</Card>
```

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — missing gap-0, so the default Card gap-6 pushes the table down
<Card className="mt-6">
  <CardHeader className="gap-3 border-b py-4 pb-3">…</CardHeader>
  <DataTable /* ... */ />
</Card>
```

Any inline status banner shown between the header and table (error/empty notice)
must also use `border-b px-6 py-3` so it reads as a continuation of the divider,
not a gap.
